# arena_mmap.tkr — the §16 arena-over-mmap keystone sub-crumb D fixture. `main.tks` runs the whole
# arena gate over the raw mmap `fundo`: the word seam (`load_u64`/`store_u64` round trips), the
# chunk/region/allocation core (distinct 16-aligned pointers sharing a chunk, a >64 KB exclusive
# chunk, zero-size distinctness, drop reclaim, idempotent sweep), the subtree sweep, the per-region
# register/lookup, the checkpoint push/pop/commit stack past depth 64, both halves of the
# `TEKO_MEM_PARANOID` poison oracle, the volume packing/reclaim proof, AND the META-POOL header-reuse
# assert (a drop-then-new region lands on the SAME header address). Every check asserts an observable
# — an address, a chunk count, a registry membership, a poisoned word — never the mere absence of a
# crash. All-pass reports exit code 42; any other code names the invariant that broke.

Feature: arena_mmap — the §16 Teko arena core over raw mmap/munmap, exit 42 on all-pass

  Scenario: full_arena_gate_over_mmap_passes — the word seam, core, subtree, registry, checkpoints, oracle, volume and META-POOL header reuse all hold
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 42
